🛠 Prerequisites
Ensure the following are installed on your local machine:
Java 21 (Required for Virtual Threads support).
Docker Desktop (To run the infrastructure stack).
Node.js & npm (For the Frontend dashboard).
Maven (For backend dependency management).
🏗 Setup Instructions
1. Infrastructure Orchestration
Spin up the required database and caching engines using the provided Docker configuration.
# From the project root
docker-compose up -d
This will initialize:
PostgreSQL (Port 5432)
Redis Stack (Port 6379 & 8001 for RedisInsight)
2. Vector Engine Initialization
The system requires the pgvector extension to handle multidimensional embeddings.
For Windows Users (Manual Build): If you are not using the Docker-preconfigured vector image, you must build pgvector manually:
Open x64 Native Tools Command Prompt as Administrator.
Navigate to the pgvector/ directory
.
Run nmake /f Makefile.win and nmake /f Makefile.win install.
In your SQL client (e.g., pgAdmin), execute:
3. Backend Configuration
Update your src/main/resources/application.yml with your LLM provider credentials (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic) and ensure the datasource points to the Docker-provisioned Postgres instance.
Build and Run:
mvn clean install
mvn spring-boot:run
4. Frontend Deployment
The dashboard provides a real-time view of the gateway's performance
.
cd Frontend
npm install
npm run dev
